# `.profile/` is NO LONGER ignored, as of 2026-09-18. It holds the operator-specific material --
# preferences, growth, tracker voice, harness manifest -- that is what lets `foundations/` stay
# standalone and portable, and it is bound for a private operator repository, so it has to be
# committable rather than hidden.
#
# ⚠️ UN-IGNORING IS NOT MOVING. This repository's only remote is public. The first push to a
# public `origin` publishes the folder, and a later `git rm` does not retract a published commit.
# Point a private remote at the work BEFORE the commit lands, not after.
#
# `.memory/` and `.workgroup/` moved to the workbench home at `~/.workbench/<org>/` on 2026-09-16
# and are no longer in this tree, so their rules were removed rather than left behind: an ignore
# rule is not the same as absence, and keeping a rule for a directory that cannot appear describes
# the tree wrongly.

# Employer-specific discipline USED to be ignored here. It is not any more -- it moved to
# `~/.workbench/<org>/foundations/` on 2026-09-16, so there is nothing to hide and no rule
# to write. The lesson is worth keeping: an ignore rule in a public repository is itself
# published, so a rule naming the org leaks the identifier the folder exists to protect.
# Ignoring something is not the same as it being absent, and only the second is private.

# ── OS and editor droppings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Duplicated from the repository root on purpose. This package is handed to adopters as a
# standalone unit, so its own ignore file has to stand up without the root's.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# ── Machine-local overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `*.local` / `*.local.*` is the conventional marker for a file that belongs to ONE bench and
# must never travel. The two `settings.local.json` files below are the exception and are
# negated: they are reference copies an adopter is meant to receive, not local overrides.
#
# Negation is required because these patterns are UNANCHORED and so match the name at any depth
# -- the same shape that once silently swallowed `templates/layout/`, whose whole purpose is to
# be committed. The failure was invisible until something checked. Anchor with a leading slash,
# or negate the intended survivors, but never leave it to luck.
*.local
*.local.*
!config/claude/settings.local.json
!templates/claude_home/settings.local.json
